1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
Friday arrives at Harbor Learning

2
00:00:01,660 --> 00:00:02,120
Circle.

3
00:00:02,370 --> 00:00:04,260
Morgan has a draft Session Option Brief

4
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:05,990
and a careful correction from last week.

5
00:00:06,260 --> 00:00:08,010
But imagine Morgan is out for an hour.

6
00:00:08,310 --> 00:00:09,150
Where is the brief?

7
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:11,080
Which source note did the preparation

8
00:00:11,130 --> 00:00:11,640
role read?

9
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:15,445
Who can answer a question about the unconfirmed
facilitator?

10
00:00:15,701 --> 00:00:21,397
If the answer lives only in Morgan's head, our
carefully designed pieces still do not make an
operating system.

11
00:00:21,674 --> 00:00:24,421
We need one page that shows how the work
travels.

12
00:00:24,771 --> 00:00:26,606
Start with the real sequence on paper.

13
00:00:26,862 --> 00:00:30,233
A request to compare a free digital-skills
session enters.

14
00:00:30,446 --> 00:00:33,454
A routing rule assigns the evidence-comparison
role.

15
00:00:33,774 --> 00:00:37,346
That role reads the three Harbor course notes
and prepares a draft.

16
00:00:37,632 --> 00:00:40,427
The draft and its short trace wait for Morgan.

17
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:45,184
Morgan may propose the option to the team, ask
for another date, or hold it.

18
00:00:45,483 --> 00:00:49,639
The agent has no route to announce, book, buy,
or send anything.

19
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:52,451
Draw that sequence before adding another box.

20
00:00:52,801 --> 00:00:55,745
Chapter Eight gives the operating map five
columns.

21
00:00:55,958 --> 00:00:58,326
Trigger: what actually starts this row?

22
00:00:58,603 --> 00:01:00,523
Role: who owns this step?

23
00:01:00,822 --> 00:01:02,728
Tier: what may that role do?

24
00:01:03,012 --> 00:01:06,724
Handoff: who receives the work next, including
a refusal?

25
00:01:07,023 --> 00:01:09,519
Evidence: where can a human find the record?

26
00:01:09,796 --> 00:01:10,970
A blank is useful.

27
00:01:11,162 --> 00:01:14,388
If you cannot name the evidence location, write
'missing.'

28
00:01:14,635 --> 00:01:18,283
A tidy imaginary location would hide the work
you still need to design.

29
00:01:18,633 --> 00:01:20,873
Put the earlier lessons onto those rows.

30
00:01:21,278 --> 00:01:23,475
The job sits at the preparation step.

31
00:01:23,667 --> 00:01:25,502
The Decision Card sits with Morgan.

32
00:01:25,801 --> 00:01:28,861
Source IDs and expiry checks sit at intake.

33
00:01:29,147 --> 00:01:31,451
The receipt and trace travel with the brief.

34
00:01:31,707 --> 00:01:36,187
Last week's correction remains a memory
proposal, pending Morgan's separate approval.

35
00:01:36,529 --> 00:01:39,961
The controller's route is a written rule, not a
new decision maker.

36
00:01:40,278 --> 00:01:45,291
A new teammate should be able to point to each
item without asking who remembers where it
went.

37
00:01:45,641 --> 00:01:51,755
The workbook also asks where approval, spend
checks, public-safe proof, and rollback sit.

38
00:01:52,066 --> 00:01:55,458
This classroom workflow has no spending or
public export.

39
00:01:55,736 --> 00:02:00,898
Mark those as closed paths with an owner, not
as empty arrows that imply they might work.

40
00:02:01,154 --> 00:02:05,858
Rollback here means Morgan can withdraw a draft
recommendation and record why.

41
00:02:06,123 --> 00:02:09,473
It does not undo an announcement, because no
announcement happens.

42
00:02:09,793 --> 00:02:14,443
If your own paper map has a step without a
named owner or a return path, circle it.

43
00:02:14,699 --> 00:02:16,406
That is the next design task.

44
00:02:16,756 --> 00:02:17,430
Pause.

45
00:02:17,805 --> 00:02:21,880
Could someone new find the current brief and
its source check from this page alone?

46
00:02:22,285 --> 00:02:24,120
Name the first missing handoff.

47
00:02:24,470 --> 00:02:26,817
Build the Operating Map in your Operating File.

48
00:02:27,115 --> 00:02:29,302
Use a fictional or approved example.

49
00:02:29,653 --> 00:02:32,192
Do not use private operational data.

50
00:02:32,512 --> 00:02:34,859
Give every row the five columns.

51
00:02:35,115 --> 00:02:40,704
Place the job, decision, source, receipt,
memory proposal, and human owner.

52
00:02:41,003 --> 00:02:45,252
Label closed paths for spending, publication,
and external messages.

53
00:02:45,533 --> 00:02:52,125
Then trace one failed source check: the note is
stale, the draft stops, and Morgan receives a
reason.

54
00:02:52,445 --> 00:02:54,728
We are making a design someone can review.

55
00:03:40,078 --> 00:03:42,057
Save revision five as a draft.

56
00:03:42,371 --> 00:03:48,003
A map earns its place when its blank cells stay
visible and someone owns each repair.

57
00:03:48,623 --> 00:03:50,203
Next we will write the permission slip

58
00:03:50,253 --> 00:03:52,303
for the preparation role and ask whether

59
00:03:52,343 --> 00:03:53,993
that work still deserves a place in the

60
00:03:54,033 --> 00:03:54,393
system.
